    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "The short answer",
      "items": [
        "Two runners exist",
        "A legacy scheduler started at boot runs every five minutes for SLA sweeps, digests, reports, callback retries and mailbox polling",
        "A newer workflow sweep is an authenticated endpoint run each minute by an external trigger that this repository does not define"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Not shown here",
      "items": [
        "SLA sweeps and notifications (the scheduler calls the SLA, Ticket, Notifier and Audit modules), the Graph mailbox the poll reads, callback retries, and the other domain modules",
        "Connected but out of scope: Auth.js sessions, Context and guards, API key service, REST API /api/v1, Inbound webhook routes, Unified intake"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "orange",
      "title": "Risks",
      "items": [
        "The workflow maintenance endpoint has no caller inside this repository, and the legacy scheduler has no HTTP trigger at all: the docs name an external cron-job.org schedule and record that it was not configured at the 2026-09-30 release; vercel.json declares no crons; the legacy sweeps run from a setInterval that only advances while a serverless instance is warm (an inference from the files)",
        "Redis is provisioned and configured but nothing reads it: config reads REDIS_URL, compose starts a container and next.config lists bullmq and ioredis as external, yet neither package is a dependency and no source file imports them"
      ]
    }
  ]
